The daemon is alive and listening, but explicitly configured as **authoritative-only** with recursion disabled. Every external DNS lookup (e.g. `google.com`) returns `REFUSED` with `recursion not available`. Internal zone (`jeremysitlab.com`) still resolves, and direct-IP communication works fine — which exactly matches the user's report that "things inside the office still work."

